 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>XI-IATI-EC_INTPA-2020-PCC-411081</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">APSA IV Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;In line with the JAES and the MoU on P&amp;S&amp;amp;G, the basic assumption upon which this Action relies is that if an effective support is provided to African organisations that have a mandate to promote peace and security, then a more effective strategy and action for peace and stability in Africa will be achieved. This Action aims to contribute, in particular, towards the achievement of SDG 16 and will be pursued through the AU and RECs/RMs. It does so with the understanding that there can be no decisive and sustainable African-led peace and security initiatives without having the proper structures, mechanisms and policy guidelines in place at both continental and regional levels. It also acknowledges the importance of aligning and intensifying the cooperation between these two levels of intervention.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The overall objective of the Action is to reduce the incidence, duration and intensity of violent conflicts in Africa.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The specific objectives (SO&#xbf;s) are that:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;SO1: The conflict cycle management under APSA is improved, with a focus on effective Early Warning Systems and the African Standby Force.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;SO2: The effectiveness of cooperation within and around the APSA framework (including with CSOs) is enhanced.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;SO3: The APSA is more inclusive of youth and children.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The expected outputs are that:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.1.1: The existing continental and regional Early Warning Systems are reinforced and interconnected;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.1.2: The multidimensional (military, civilian and police) capacity of the African Standby Force is enhanced;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.1.3: The continental and regional strategic Planning Elements of the African Standby Force are strengthened and interconnected&lt;a href=&quot;#_ftn1&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[1]&lt;/a&gt;;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.1.4: AU (including ACSRT/AFRIPOL)/RECs/RMs strategies and capacities to address transnational organised crime, terrorism and violent extremism as well as climate change risks to peace and security are harmonised and enhanced;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.1.5: Geo-specific Post Conflict Reconstruction and Development strategies and capacities for priority areas are developed;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.2.1: AU/RECs/RMs coordination and cooperation mechanisms on APSA are strengthened internally as well as externally with the EU and CSOs;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.2.2: The operational and reporting capacities of the AU/RECs/RMs on the APSA are enhanced and harmonised;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.3.1: The AU Youth Peace and Security Strategy 2020-2024 is fully developed;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.3.2: Youth opportunities for interaction on APSA with AU/RECs/RMs are facilitated;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&#xb7;O.3.3: The rights, protection and welfare of Children Affected by Armed Conflicts (CAAC) are mainstreamed into the APSA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
